---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ReviewedByCard from "../../components/ReviewedByCard.astro";
import { TRUST_PROFILES } from "../../config/trust";

const title = "HOA Fees and Mortgage Payment (How to model them)";
const description =
  "Model HOA dues, assessment risk, and insurance gaps as housing costs that affect affordability without changing loan amortization. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-04-22";
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/guides/hoa-fees-and-mortgage-payment"
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
  authorProfile={TRUST_PROFILES.siteOwner}
  reviewProfiles={[TRUST_PROFILES.editorialReview, TRUST_PROFILES.methodologyReview]}
  robots="noindex, follow"
>
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">HOA fees</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>HOA fees and your mortgage payment</h1>
    <p>
      This page is for the buyer whose mortgage looks affordable until HOA dues, special assessments, or condo insurance gaps are
      layered into the actual monthly housing burden.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">DTI calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/mortgage-payment-affordability-checklist">Affordability checklist</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ReviewedByCard
    writtenBy={TRUST_PROFILES.siteOwner}
    reviewedBy={TRUST_PROFILES.editorialReview}
    secondaryReview={TRUST_PROFILES.methodologyReview}
    reviewScope="HOA housing-cost review, assessment-risk framing, and routing between DTI, affordability, and housing-payment composition."
    reviewedOn={lastUpdated}
  />

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Use this guide when HOA dues are the missing part of the housing-payment estimate</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Use this page when the mortgage looks manageable until recurring association costs are added back in.</li>
      <li>If you need the full payment formula first, move to <a href="/guides/how-mortgage-payments-are-calculated">how mortgage payments are calculated</a>.</li>
      <li>If the next question is lender qualification, move next to <a href="/guides/mortgage-payment-dti-housing-payment">mortgage payment in DTI calculations</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Why HOA is easy to underestimate</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      HOA behaves like housing cost but not loan amortization. It does not reduce principal, it does not appear in the loan balance,
      and that is exactly why buyers sometimes forget how powerfully it changes cash flow and DTI.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Base dues tell only part of the story</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li>Recurring dues should always be added to the housing payment.</li>
        <li>Historic increases matter because low current dues can rise.</li>
        <li>Budget weakness can show up through later fee hikes.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">The hidden risk is often not the dues line</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li>special assessment risk can matter more than the base dues.</li>
        <li>master policy can still leave personal coverage gaps.</li>
        <li>Reserve underfunding can turn into future monthly strain.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">The comparison that keeps people honest</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Compare the same home with and without HOA included in the housing payment.</li>
      <li>Then stress test one assessment or dues increase scenario.</li>
      <li>That shows whether the home is truly affordable or only looks acceptable when association costs are ignored.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">When to move to a different page</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>If the question is DTI treatment, move to <a href="/guides/mortgage-payment-dti-housing-payment">mortgage payment in DTI calculations</a>.</li>
      <li>If the issue is insurance composition, move to <a href="/guides/mortgage-payment-insurance-assumptions">mortgage payment insurance assumptions</a>.</li>
      <li>If the real issue is whether the total payment still fits, move to <a href="/guides/mortgage-payment-affordability-checklist">mortgage payment affordability checklist</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">References</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/consumer-tools/mortgages/ready-to-buy-a-home/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Ready to buy a home?
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/owning-a-home/explore/home-loan-toolkit/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Your home loan toolkit
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Run the mortgage payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">Check DTI</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/mortgage-payment-affordability-checklist">Affordability checklist</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-04-22</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
